// A function value handed back through TWO inferred returns. `vl check` returns 0 and the
// emitter declared `deliver`'s result `i32` while its body pushed a closure ref — check-clean
// INVALID WASM with an annotated receiver, and `emitProgram: call to unknown function` with an
// un-annotated one: one missing rung, two clauses.
//
// `blockTailIsClosure` asked only `exprIsClosureNoLocal`, whose arms are `Paren`, `FuncDecl`,
// `Ident` and `ObjLit` — no `Call`. One hop is fine, because `exprIsClosure`'s own `Call` arm
// asks `fnReturnsClosure`; it is the SECOND hop, in return position where only the restricted
// predicate is available, that had nothing to ask. The arena carries the answer (the checker
// records `(i32) => i32` for the tail), so the rung is one structural read with no recursion
// bound to get right. See D1620. Should print 55.
function mk() { return (n: i32) => n + 1 }
function deliver() { return mk() }
const v: (i32) => i32 = deliver()
print(v(54))
